  "chapter": 764,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 85 Chapter 764\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4548, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the social services law, in relation to providing\n        for  the  automated  identification  of  affordability   program\n        participants\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill would direct the Office of Temporary and Disability Assist-\nance (OTDA) to automatically identify and match  recipients  of  certain\npublic  benefits  with the accounts of utilities customers for potential\nparticipation in utility-operated  energy  affordability  programs.  The\nbill  would  authorize  OTDA  to delegate the matching to other state or\nlocal entities, allowing existing programs to continue.\n \n  I am committed to ensuring every  New  Yorker  can  live  in  a  safe,\ndecent,  and  affordable  home. Low- and moderate-income New Yorkers may\nnot be aware of energy affordability programs, or they may  have  diffi-\nculty  applying  to  these  programs. By automatically identifying which\nutility customers receive certain public benefits and  thus  are  likely\neligible  for  energy  affordability  programs,  this bill would make it\neasier for New Yorkers to affordably power  their  homes.  However,  the\nlegislation  would  require  several  changes  to  avoid potential legal\nissues or undue administrative burdens and to facilitate  the  effective\nimplementation of the automatic matching.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2023
 },
